+ * the colour where a = 1, and the conversion back to codes of the transport then takes nothing of
+ * the picture under it (its second term is (1 - a) times a finite value: 0). Such a tile is packed
+ * once as before, into a texture of the packer's (with a check that every one of its pixels came
+ * out of the composite with an alpha of exactly 1), and from the next frame on its bytes are
+ * copied from there: passes 3, 8 and 4 are not drawn in it, until a texel that it may read
+ * changes, or what the codes of those pixels are made with does: the metadata's representation
+ * (dvbridge_source_params), the level of the conversion under the GUI of a picture whose decoding
+ * is not affine, the size of the GUI texture, or the key of its composite. The tiles of the first
+ * row of the raster (that hold the metadata) are never kept. The same bytes as packing them again,
+ * for any picture under them. Off until asked for (use), and only where the caller gives the key
+ * of its composite (dvbridge_source_drawn_key()); without the programs it needs, off. */
